The function has no docstring, and `timedelta` is used but not imported. I'll add the docstring and keep the change limited to that, noting the missing import in the summary rather than silently fixing it. [tool_use propose_change {"path":"register/dates.py","summary":"Add docstring to consultation_end explaining the default 21-day consultation period. Note: `timedelta` is used but not imported in this file; I have not changed that.","diff":"--- a/register/dates.py\n+++ b/register/dates.py\n@@ -1,3 +1,14 @@\n # register/dates.py\n def consultation_end(received, days=21):\n+    \"\"\"Return the consultation end date for an application.\n+\n+    The consultation period runs for 21 days from the date the application\n+    was received, so the default `days=21` gives the standard consultation\n+    window. Pass a different `days` value only where a non-standard period\n+    applies.\n+\n+    Args:\n+        received: The date the application was received.\n+        days: Length of the consultation period in days. Defaults to 21.\n+    \"\"\"\n     return received + timedelta(days=days)\n"}]
